    {
      "id": "f-vertex-bone-weights-facade",
      "name": "FVertexBoneWeightsFacade",
      "category": "CollectionVertexBoneWeightsFacade",
      "signature": "FVertexBoneWeightsFacade(In Self)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "In Self",
          "type": "FManagedArrayCollection&"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "Void",
      "docs": "FVertexBoneWeightsFacade\nDefines common API for storing a vertex weights bound to a bone. This mapping is from the\nthe vertex to the bone index. Kinematic array specifies whether vertices are considered kinematic.\nNon-kinematic vertices can also have associated bone indices and weights.\nThen arrays can be accessed later by:\nconst TManagedArray< TArray<int32> >* BoneIndices = FVertexBoneWeightsFacade::GetBoneIndices(this);\nconst TManagedArray< TArray<float> >* BoneWeights = FVertexBoneWeightsFacade::GetBoneWeights(this);\nThe following attributes are created on the collection:\n- FindAttribute<TArray<int32>>(FVertexSetInterface::IndexAttribute, FGeometryCollection::VerticesGroup);\n- FindAttribute<TArray<float>>(FVertexSetInterface::WeightAttribute, FGeometryCollection::VerticesGroup);"
    },
